  "texts": [
    "Did you know your fridge doesn't actually make any cold?",
    "Instead, it pumps heat out of its inside.",
    "Its hidden pipes carry a special substance called refrigerant.",
    "It boils at just minus twelve degrees.",
    "As it evaporates, it soaks up heat from your food.",
    "It's the same way sweat cools you as it dries.",
    "Then the compressor at the bottom back squeezes the gas.",
    "Squeezed gas gets hot, hotter than your kitchen.",
    "The grille on the back hands that heat to the room.",
    "The gas cools down and turns back into liquid.",
    "A narrow tube drops its pressure, and it turns cold again.",
    "Then the whole cycle repeats over and over again.",
    "That's why your fridge feels warm at the back.",
    "An open fridge won't cool your kitchen, it warms it.",
    "Follow for more physics hiding in your kitchen!"
  ]
